      "writtenOn": "2025-07-28T11:54:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e \u003e Well, did you check the return value of the \"git verify-tag\" command you gave?\n\u003e \u003e I suspect it\u0027s non-zero, indicating a failed signature verification.\n\u003e \n\u003e I didn\u0027t check this before. You are right that it\u0027s non-zero:\n\nGood :-) So I got that bit actually right when I wrote the JGit code.\n\nWhatever Gerrit does, _client-side_ signature verification of such a signed tag might still fail unless the user provides an allowedSigners file containing the public key. \n\nThe tag message of a signed tag _must_ end with \\n; JGit enforces that at [1]. The REST API should probably verify that and accept only input where the message _does_ end with LF if a signature is also given.\n\n[1] https://github.com/eclipse-jgit/jgit/blob/ca6d673d59f27382758e1f54e7731b9d658a5730/org.eclipse.jgit/src/org/eclipse/jgit/api/TagCommand.java#L239",
      "parentUuid": "2a6007ed_665f1ce4",
